meta {
  name: Unknown class - 200 with empty results
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

get {
  url: {{newBase}}/competitions/{{compId}}/classresults?class=NoSuchClass
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  class: NoSuchClass
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
}

docs {
A class that does not exist returns `200` with `results: []` rather than an error.

  This looked dangerous — `insertResults` ends with a `notInArray` sweep that
  soft-deletes stored rows missing from the incoming set, so an empty set reads like
  it would wipe the class.

  It does not. `insertResults` returns early when the parsed list is empty, ahead of
  the sweep, so an empty payload is a no-op. Proved by
  `server/tests/live-class-writer.test.ts` ("an empty result list is a no-op, not a
  mass soft-delete"), and the plan was corrected accordingly — no client-side guard
  is needed.
}
